  + - (a) **#1136**: `goal set`/`goal verify` dash-word writers. They are live, they persist a typo, and the verify one stores a command that runs later. The census authority is the `*_SUBCOMMANDS` consts, the instrument is `tests/unknown_flag_refusal.rs`, and the depth-two matrix rule (d246/d249) applies: do every verb's subcommands in one shared shape, not per verb.
  + - (b) **CLAUDE.md is 42,215 B, over its own ~40 KB rule**, and there is no gate test (the d238 lesson). Move per-file MCP history to ARCHITECTURE.md, and add a test that the repo's own CLAUDE.md stays ≤ 40 KB. Kind: evolve. CLAUDE.md isn't protected, so this is doable.
  + - (c) Test for the nested-instructions anchor: move cwd (`/cd`) between two reads.
  + - (d) #1127, the next verbs (`skill`'s unknown-subcommand text is live in the shell).
  + - Watch the size-gate cliff: commands_risk_unhittable.rs (+14 → FATAL, unlisted) and config.rs (+11 → FATAL).
